{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>If Your face does not go, etc.</b> He was not satisfied with HaShem's word, and said: Is it for this thing that I pray? <b>If Your face does not go</b> from now on, they are lost, and there is no need for their ascent. <b>And whereby shall it be known then that I have found favor</b>, etc. — <b>Is it not in Your going with us</b>, meaning, the supernal aspect, which is the sod of the Great Light, called by the name of the blessed הויה — not Your face alone, which is the aspect of the Throne. And what You promised me, that this aspect would be mine alone, as He said <b>and I will grant you rest</b> — I ask that it also govern all of us together, I and Your people, and that is His saying <b>and we shall be distinguished, I and Your people</b>, by the measure of mercy and the supremely exalted attribute above which there is none higher. And El Elyon was reconciled and said to him: <b>Also this thing</b> which you have spoken I will do, to govern them by the aspect of the complete Name, the unified One, blessed be He — <b>for you have found</b>, etc., meaning, not by the merit of Israel but by the finding of your favor."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:36:27.796692398Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}